{# ═══ CORNER STACK (homepage only) ═══
   Jack, 2026-08-24: move "Texas compliance" out of the announcement bar
   and down into a fixed bottom-right widget, paired with a back-to-top
   control. Scoped to "/" only — every other page keeps the compliance
   link in the top bar (see nav.njk). Hidden until the visitor has
   scrolled roughly past the hero (main.js), so it doesn't compete with
   the hero on first paint. The compliance button needs no new JS: it
   carries the same [data-compliance-open] attribute the announce-bar
   link used, and the shared dialog wiring in main.js binds to every
   element with that attribute, wherever it lives. #}
<div class="corner-stack" id="corner-stack">
  <button class="corner-row" type="button" data-compliance-open>
    <span>Texas compliance</span>
  </button>
  <button class="corner-row" type="button" id="back-to-top">
    <svg class="corner-icon corner-arrow" width="15" height="15" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg>
    <span>Back to top</span>
  </button>
</div>
